{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem was in `backoff_delay`: the docstring promised a cap, but the implementation only computed `base * 2**attempt`, so high attempts blew past `cap` (e.g. attempt 10 with base 1 returned 1024 instead of 60).\n\n**Change:** apply the cap with `min(base * (2 ** attempt), cap)`.\n\n`retry_summary` in `repo/rows.py` already builds schedules from `backoff_delay`, so no change there. After the fix, a 12-retry run looks like `[1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 60, 60, …]` with total wait 423s.\n\n`old_backoff` is still a thin alias around `backoff_delay` with default `base`/`cap`; it inherits the fixed behavior. Both visible tests pass."}]},"session_id":"70b51a1d-17b4-44db-be00-4a0dc6730bc1"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":45789,"duration_api_ms":45789,"is_error":false,"result":"Reviewing `repo/backoff.py` and related retry/backoff helpers.\n\n\nApplying the cap in `backoff_delay` and removing the stale bug comment.\n\n\nThe problem was in `backoff_delay`: the docstring promised a cap, but the implementation only computed `base * 2**attempt`, so high attempts blew past `cap` (e.g. attempt 10 with base 1 returned 1024 instead of 60).\n\n**Change:** apply the cap with `min(base * (2 ** attempt), cap)`.\n\n`retry_summary` in `repo/rows.py` already builds schedules from `backoff_delay`, so no change there. After the fix, a 12-retry run looks like `[1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 60, 60, …]` with total wait 423s.\n\n`old_backoff` is still a thin alias around `backoff_delay` with default `base`/`cap`; it inherits the fixed behavior. Both visible tests pass.","session_id":"70b51a1d-17b4-44db-be00-4a0dc6730bc1","request_id":"778b5ba6-4d1f-450c-9cbe-d6ccfbdfb03a","usage":{"inputTokens":12873,"outputTokens":1639,"cacheReadTokens":79253,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
